id: pm-gh1741
title: "GH-1741: pm create rewrites a positional title such as \"Docs: adopt X\" into an option, and the refusal repeats the failed command"
description: "GitHub issue 1741 (opened 2026-11-16). On pm 2026.11.16, a positional create title that starts with a create option name followed by a colon, such as \"Docs: adopt X\", \"Release:\", \"Test:\", \"Files:\", \"Comment:\" or \"Note:\", is rewritten into that option before parsing. The cause is parseBareKeyValueToken in src/sdk/cli-bootstrap.ts: it promotes any Name:value or Name=value token whose name resolves to a canonical flag, so \"Docs: adopt X\" becomes --doc \" adopt X\". The title is lost. pm create issue then refuses with create_positional_type_without_title, and its next step repeats the attempted command. The RFC 9457 title also cuts the refusal message mid-command at 120 characters. The issue asks for four changes. First, a single argv element with whitespace after Word: is a title, never shorthand. Second, the remaining shorthand is limited to whitespace-free tokens, and the error names the rewrite. Third, next_steps never suggests the command just attempted and offers --title instead. Fourth, the title does not cut off a command. Duplicate check: searched positional title Docs: Release: prefix rewritten into option create; the related closed items are pm-7vm9 and pm-8sr3 (positional title support)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
