comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T16:55:16.674Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation note (2026-11-16): parseBareKeyValueToken now returns null for a colon token that contains any whitespace, so a shell-grouped token such as \"Docs: adopt X\" stays text, while whitespace-free shorthand (docs:README.md) and the equals form keep their promotion. main.ts records the invocation's bare_key_value promotions in src/cli/runtime/invocation-rewrites.ts. The create positional-type refusal names each promoted token and suggests renderPmCommand([create, <type>, --title, <token>]), and otherwise suggests the --title form, never the attempted command. Its message was shortened to stay within the 120-character problem title. Verified on a scratch tracker: all six listed prefixes create Issues with their titles intact, and pm create issue Docs:README refuses with next step 'Keep \"Docs:README\" as the title: pm create issue --title Docs:README'."
